{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And the eyes of my brother Benjamin.</b> The meaning: if you do not wish to tell on account of the oaths — behold, Benjamin my brother, who was not under the oath, he will tell Father. Another interpretation: even Benjamin has reason to worry more than you do, lest I die, for since he was not involved in selling me, he might not believe my words — <b>for the mouth that speaks to you</b> — until now the interpreter was between us."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 45, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:08:39.589335724Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}